Wow, Valkeries are way easier to ascend than Wizards.  After I
ascended my wizard (I had many wizards die before I finally got to
ascend one), I ascended on my 3rd Valkerie.  The first Valkerie died
in the quest level by getting hit by a drawbridge.  I thought the only
drawbridge in the game was on the castle level.  The game defintly
waited for me to walk on the drawbridge square before zapping a wand
at the drawbridge.  The second Valkerie died early in the game by a
rabid rat.  I'm sure I did something really stupid, but I forgot what
I did.  The third Valkerie got ascended (that's this Valkerie).  Here
is the story....

I started the game by having me and my pet gain a couple of levels.  I
disarmed a dart trap and took the darts.  I then went straight to
Sokoban.  I like going to Sokoban before the Gnomish mines for a
couple of reasons... 1) it gives me a chance to get telepathy before
going to the mines.  2) it gives me a chance to find a unicorn horn in
Sokoban.  Since unicorns can't teleport in Sokoban, I actually have a
chance to kill them in Sokoban.  3) Guaranteed food.  4) Guaranteed
scrolls of earth.  5) possible amulet of reflection (which is really
important since I don't have magic resistance yet).  6) pushing the
Sokoban boulders boosts strength.  Yeah, Sokoban is good.  I found a
wand of death in Sokoban.  I would rather have gotten a fast
engravable wand because I'm not about to use up my death wand this
early in the game.  A fast engravable wand can get a hoard of monsters
off you in 1 turn.  A wand of death can only be shot in one direction
per turn.  I went to the top level of Sokoban.  The top level is the
version that gives a bag of holding, so I left Sokoban.

I went down to the Gnomish Mine Town.  I found mytheral armor along
the way.  I'm not finding very many daggers, so I'm still relying on
my darts for ranged attacks.   I think all my pets are large sized
now.  I let my pets attack the peaceful law enforcement, because they
usually drop decent armor (mainly I need them for gloves, since not
much else drops gloves this early in the game).  All my pets ended up
dead.  I went down to the bottom of the mines and got the engravable
gems and the luckstone.  Getting to the botom of the mines is really
easy when you are a dwarf since most of the mines monsters are
peaceful toward dwarves.  I found a magic lamp somewhere in the Mines,
but I'm not about to use any wishes anytime soon because I don't want
to wish for stuff the game might give me later.  I used one scroll of
identify to ID some of the engravable gems.  I got back to the Mine
Town easily.  I went to the general store in the mines.  I shoved all
the store inventory in the corner.  I usually like to drop a cursed
item on the pile so pets won't take from that pile.  I sold the IDed
engravable gems and had my new pet get my gems back.  I bought some
protection from the mine town priest.

During the game I'll uncurse all the cursed rings I find by dipping
them in fountains.  I'll try on all the uncursed rings to look for a
levitation ring.  The other rings aren't worth IDing.

I decided that trying to polymorph my pets is a horrible idea.  This
is because polymorphed uber pets take so much of your XP that it takes
way too long to reach the required XL14 to start your character quest.
 I don't like having horses as pets because they tend to go crazy with
hunger and attack my other pets.  So I'm stuck with cruddy dogs and
cats.

I didn't want to sacrifice at all because I knew I wanted to wish for
Grayswander.  I needed the number of artifacts created in the game to
be at most 1 so that my artifact wish would be guaranteed.  However, I
knew I was defintly going to get my quest artifact before I got the
wand of wishing.  Since sacrificing runs the risk of getting an
artifact as a reward, I couldn't sacrifice until I got Grayswander.

I lost my telepathy.  I thought you lost telepathy by killing your own
race, but apparently you lose telepathy by killing a peaceful human
when you aren't chaotic.  I went around looking for another floating
eye corpse so I could get my telepathy back.  Then I decided to tin
any floating eye corpses I find in case I lose telepathy again.

I got a unicorn horn, so now I can easily eat the corpses that give
the poison resistance instrinsic.  Got poison resistance.  I got cold
resistance fairly soon afterwards.

I had two swords now.  One really corroded sword for rust monsters,
and my regular sword.

I went nymph hunting to get their object detection potions.  Then I
used those potions to find the Fort portal.  I'm not about to go
through the Fort level without magic resistance or reflection because
I usually get zapped with a wand of death by one of the many soldiers
on the Fort level.

Found a room full of leperchauns and tinned some of them so I could
get their teleportitis instrinsic later in the game (after I find
teleport control).

I found a shield of reflection in a shop around DL19.

Even though I only have dumpy pets, I'm still only XL12.  I still
don't have a way to walk over water.  I did some Incubus dancing until
I got boosted up to XL14.

Got fire resistance in the first level of the quest.  I started
tinning all the giant corpses so I could gain all their strength
bonuses.  The quest was super easy .  I still didn't have a way to
walk over water, so I hesitated to walk over any ice squares because
monsters in the Valkerie like to blast the ice with fire rays.  This
time I refused to walk over the drawbridge since there are a bunch of
monsters in the mini-castle that might have a wand of striking.  The
quest nemesis teleported next to me and I zapped him with my wand of
death.  I heard the Valkerie quest nemesis is easy to kill, but I
don't have an amulet of life saving yet so I'm not taking any chances.

Went to Medusa's level.  Still can't cross all the water in this
level.  Dug a hole and fell to the below level.  Walked up the stairs
to the middle of Medusa's castle.  Medusa's castle had a shield of
reflection instead of levitation boots.

Invoked my quest artifact until I got teleported above Medusa's level.
 I used my magic lamp to wish for a cloak of magic resistance. 
Cleared out the Fort level.  I had to push a boulder to make a ghetto
bridge to get in the Fort.  I took the money and bought more divine
protection.  I got silver dragon scale mail from the Fort level.  I
think I got shock resistance from a blue dragon on the Fort level.

Went to the castle.  I used my mastermind skills to figure out the
passkey to open the castle drawbridge.  Then I ran to the maze-like
section on the left size of the level.  I went to a spot in the
maze-like section such that monsters can only see me when they are in
melee range.  I was hoping that monsters only summon creatures when
you are in sight range, so I'd have a good chance of killing them
before they summoned anything.  Since there were 'L' monsters on the
level, everything on the level would be "aware of my presense" and
come running at me.  I killed all the 'L' monsters without any of them
summoning anything.  I pushed a couple of boulders into the trap doors
so I could reach the section of the castle with the 4 ghetto abandoned
shop areas.

It's official.  The ascension kit the game gave me is a shirt and
silver dragon scale mail.  Whatever.  I need to go through my mass
cleanup of the dungeon now.  I went through and collected all the
scrolls, potions, and magic items I could carry.  I dropped them in
adjacent 5 piles on the Fort level.  The 5th pile (in the doorway) is
the 15 page pile of dead soldier junk.  I only had 2 wands of
polymorph, so I couldn't polypile the hell out of everything like when
I was a wizard.  I got speed boots and a couple of rings.  I used the
wand to wish for 2 blessed charging scrolls, +2 Grayswander, and 2
magic markers.

I really don't care that I don't have gauntlets of power or a helm of
brillance.  I'm not using the stupid hammer artifact so I don't need
gauntlets of power.  I only have 10MP so the helm of brillance won't
do much either.

I polymorphed into a winged gargoyle and blanked a bunch of
potions/scrolls.  I went up to DL1 and started foo-proofing and
enchanting all my stuff.  I accidently wrote an enchant armor scroll
when I meant to write an enchant weapon scroll.  I read the scroll and
my speed boots broke.  I used my last wish for another pair of speed
boots.  I finished enchanting my gear.  I genocided mindflayers,
master mind flayers, and all 'L' monsters.  I got bumped down a couple
of XL levels.  I think polymorphing might screw up your levels.

I switched to using Grayswander and a silver saber in two-weapon
combat.  I don't think I have see invisible yet, and I probably
polypiled them all into more useful wands.  I decided to get crowned,
so I threw a couple IDed gems at an aligned.  I got crowned really
quickly.  I never got the stupid hammer artifact as a sacrifice gift
either.

Gehennom is really annoying without the magic mapping spell.  I
switched to using a pick-axe and a silver saber in two-weapon combat. 
Now I can do damage and dig through walls without having to switch
in/out Grayswander every 10 turns.  If important looking monsters show
up, I'd switch to the double saber setup.  Anything  that shows up as
a '2' from my warning ability I assumed might be a green slime.  I'd
observe how fast the '2' was moving.  If it moved too slow, I'd throw
some daggers at it.  I found out I didn't carry as many daggers into
gehennom as I thought I did.  I didn't have enough to guarantee
killing a disenchanter, so I still had to use Elbereth when they came
so I could retrieve the daggers and throw them again.

Besides the lack of magic map, I made it to the vibrating square
easily.  Zapped a light wand near the vibrating square so I could find
it later.  Right before killing the Wizard of Yendor I used the last
charges of the polymorph wand at a row of 5 amulets (1 amulet per
pile).  Got a second amulet of life saving.  Killed the Wizard of
Yendor, went through the Sanctum, zapped the Moloch priest with a
death wand, got the amulet, drank a cursed gain level potion to rise
out of the Sanctum.

Used my large collection of digging wands to quickly dig through the
Gehennom levels.  I think trying to clear paths before the ascension
run is mostly useless because you get bumped to random parts of the
levels.  I got bumped around Gehennom way too much.  Got out of
Gehennom.

Went to the Fort and collected a couple more K-rations. I made sure I
still had everything I needed, and made sure I didn't need to uncurse
any of my equipment.  Went to the Elemental planes.

The Elemental planes were way easy.  The Air Plane went slowly for my
wizard since I had to watch out for Air Elementals.  With the Valkerie
I could just make a mad dash for the portal because I could survive
getting digested by 5 Air Elementals in a row.  Double sabers do alot
of damage, and I only took half damage because of my quest artifact.

Got to Astral Plane.  Went to put on my blindfold.  Found out my
blindfold is missing.  Fortunatly an Archon blinded me in the next
turn.  Death is in the right side of the Planes, so I went to the left
side.  Used alot of teleport wand zaps, a couple of death wand zaps,
and some double sabers slicing.  The left altar was not Lawful.  Went
back to the beginning and read confused create monster scrolls to make
some acid blobs to block the path.  Zapped my way to the top altar and
it was Lawful.  Offered the amulet.  The Astral Plane is way easier
for the Valkerie than the Wizard.  Since this ascension was alot less
eventful than my last one, below I've listed the
potions/scrolls/wands/spellbooks I used so you can get a feel of my
general game stragety.


